@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-fixtures`
IMPORT `ito66-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito66-d-common-source`
IMPORT `ito66-a-separate-calculation`
IMPORT `ito66-b-property-income`
IMPORT `ito66-ab-taxable-income`
IMPORT `ito66-c-credit-points`

-- ===========================================================================
-- INDEPENDENT TESTS of the IL-02 encoding of s 66, by a second author.
--
-- Every expected value below was decided from the Hebrew source alone and
-- written down in DECIDED-ANSWERS.md (finished Tue Oct 6 14:03:09 UTC 2026)
-- before any .l4 file of the encoding was opened.  Each assertion carries the
-- scenario id from that file.  The encoding was read afterwards only to learn
-- its names and how inputs are supplied; the builders come from
-- ito66-fixtures.l4, and no expected value was taken from ito66-tests.l4 or
-- ito66-tests-ita.l4.
--
-- A failing assertion is a finding and is left failing.  Each is listed, with
-- its classification, in INDEPENDENT-FINDINGS.md.  Scenarios the interface
-- cannot express are listed there too, and named in comments below.
--
-- Amounts are invented scenario inputs in shekels.  The one figure taken from
-- the source is 2,904, the value of a credit point in 2024-2027, from the
-- editorial note in s 33A (line 1563), used in C-CAP.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Independent tests — builders`

GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
      k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What section 66(c) gives the spouse`
`fid in a separate calculation: 36A` h `; s 37` s `; children` k MEANS
    `in a separate calculation`
        (`Credit points under section 66(c)` WITH
            `one half point under section 36A, by paragraph (4)`        IS h
            `one half point under section 37, by paragraph (2)`         IS s
            `points for children, by paragraphs (4), (4A), (5) and (6)` IS k)

-- A man (registered, salaried, not claiming) and a woman (not registered,
-- salaried, claiming under (a)(1)), with one child of both.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `born`     IS A NUMBER
      `defers`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`fid couple in tax year` `the year` `, one child of both born` `born` `, mother defers` `defers` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` `the year`
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 100000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE)
        `; children`   (LIST (`a child born in tax year` `born` `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` TRUE `; mother defers a point` `defers` `; interest` 0))
        `; common source` NOTHING

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `born`     IS A NUMBER
      `defers`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What section 66(c) gives the spouse`
`fid the woman's points, tax year` `the year` `, child born` `born` `, mother defers` `defers` MEANS
    `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in`
        (`fid couple in tax year` `the year` `, one child of both born` `born` `, mother defers` `defers`)

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `born`     IS A NUMBER
      `defers`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What section 66(c) gives the spouse`
`fid the man's points, tax year` `the year` `, child born` `born` `, mother defers` `defers` MEANS
    `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `registered spouse` `in`
        (`fid couple in tax year` `the year` `, one child of both born` `born` `, mother defers` `defers`)

-- 2024: a salaried registered man (200,000, not claiming) and, not
-- registered, the given spouse; no children; no common source.
GIVEN `the other` IS A `A spouse`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`fid 2024, a salaried registered man and, not registered,` `the other` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2024
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE)
        `; other`      `the other`
        `; children`   EMPTY
        `; common source` NOTHING

-- A woman, not registered, claiming under (a)(1), whose income from personal
-- exertion is the one item given.
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `An item of income from personal exertion`
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`fid a claiming woman whose income from personal exertion is` `the item` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `a woman` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `the item`) `; other income` 0
        `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0
        `; claims under (a)` TRUE `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of income from personal exertion`
      `first`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `second`   IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fid may the woman claim, 2024, on 50,000 of` `the kind` `; limb 1` `first` `; limb 2` `second` MEANS
    `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for`
        (`fid 2024, a salaried registered man and, not registered,`
            (`fid a claiming woman whose income from personal exertion is`
                (`income of kind` `the kind` `of` 50000 `; paid for employment income that qualified:` `first` `; qualified in the five years before:` `second`)))

-- 2024: salaried registered man (200,000), salaried woman (120,000)
-- claiming under (a)(1), with the given common source.
GIVEN `source` IS A MAYBE `A common source of income`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` `source` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2024
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE)
        `; children`   EMPTY
        `; common source` `source`

-- A spouse with salary, other income, property income and the two claims.
GIVEN `the sex`   IS A `Sex`
      `salary`    IS A NUMBER
      `other`     IS A NUMBER
      `pre`       IS A NUMBER
      `inh`       IS A NUMBER
      `claims a`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `claims b`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`fid spouse` `the sex` `; salary` `salary` `; other income` `other` `; pre-marriage` `pre` `; inherited` `inh` `; claims (a)` `claims a` `; claims (b)` `claims b` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `the sex` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` `salary`) `; other income` `other`
        `; pre-marriage property income` `pre` `; inherited property income` `inh`
        `; claims under (a)` `claims a` `; claims under (b)` `claims b` `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE

GIVEN `reg`   IS A `A spouse`
      `other` IS A `A spouse`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`fid 2024 couple, registered` `reg` `, other` `other` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2024 `; registered` `reg` `; other` `other` `; children` EMPTY `; common source` NOTHING

-- A child of both spouses with the four kinds of income (a)(3) names.
GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER
      `tc`   IS A NUMBER
      `reit` IS A NUMBER
      `intr` IS A NUMBER
      `cg`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A child, for section 66`
`fid child of both born` `born` `; transparent company` `tc` `; REIT` `reit` `; interest` `intr` `; capital gain` `cg` MEANS
    `A child, for section 66` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                                     IS `born`
        `a child of the registered spouse`                      IS TRUE
        `a child of the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS TRUE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS FALSE
        `taxable income from a transparent company`             IS `tc`
        `taxable income from a real estate investment trust`    IS `reit`
        `taxable income from interest`                          IS `intr`
        `taxable income from capital gain`                      IS `cg`

-- 2024: registered man with PE `reg PE`, woman with PE `other PE` claiming,
-- the registered man holding `passive` of other income, one child.
GIVEN `reg PE`   IS A NUMBER
      `other PE` IS A NUMBER
      `passive`  IS A NUMBER
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 66`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`fid 2024, registered PE` `reg PE` `, other PE` `other PE` `, passive` `passive` `, child` `the child` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2024
        `; registered` (`fid spouse` `a man` `; salary` `reg PE` `; other income` `passive` `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` FALSE `; claims (b)` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`fid spouse` `a woman` `; salary` `other PE` `; other income` 0 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` TRUE `; claims (b)` FALSE)
        `; children`   (LIST `the child`)
        `; common source` NOTHING

-- Step-families and mixed families: the registered spouse, the other, and
-- the children, in 2024.
GIVEN `reg`   IS A `A spouse`
      `other` IS A `A spouse`
      `kids`  IS A LIST OF `A child, for section 66`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`fid 2024 family, registered` `reg` `, other` `other` `, children` `kids` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` 2024 `; registered` `reg` `; other` `other` `; children` `kids` `; common source` NOTHING

GIVEN `the sex`  IS A `Sex`
      `salary`   IS A NUMBER
      `claims`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `widowed`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `s37`      IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`fid salaried` `the sex` `earning` `salary` `; claims` `claims` `; widowed` `widowed` `; s 37` `s37` MEANS
    `a spouse:` `the sex` `; income from personal exertion` (LIST `a salary of` `salary`) `; other income` 0
        `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0
        `; claims under (a)` `claims` `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` `widowed` `; s 37` `s37`

GIVEN `born` IS A NUMBER
      `reg`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `oth`  IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `A child, for section 66`
`fid child born` `born` `; of registered` `reg` `; of other` `oth` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` `born` `; of the registered spouse` `reg` `; of the other spouse` `oth` `; mother defers a point` FALSE `; interest` 0

§ `Independent tests — V, the tax years`

-- V-1: woman, 2024, child born 2024: 2½.  (c)(4)(a) "בשנת לידתו".
#ASSERT (`fid the woman's points, tax year` 2024 `, child born` 2024 `, mother defers` FALSE) EQUALS (`fid in a separate calculation: 36A` 0.5 `; s 37` 0 `; children` 2.5)
-- V-2: the same question for tax year 2023: refused (brief; the source shows only the law at retrieval).
#ASSERT REFUSED (`fid the woman's points, tax year` 2023 `, child born` 2024 `, mother defers` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED (`fid the woman's points, tax year` 2023 `, child born` 2023 `, mother defers` FALSE)
-- V-3: man, 2027, child born 2020 (turns 7): 1.  (c)(5)(c).
#ASSERT (`fid the man's points, tax year` 2027 `, child born` 2020 `, mother defers` FALSE) EQUALS (`fid in a separate calculation: 36A` 0 `; s 37` 0 `; children` 1)
-- V-4: the (a)(1) claim in tax year 2023: refused.  Asked of the (a)(1) entitlement rule, and of the assembled calculation.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid couple in tax year` 2023 `, one child of both born` 2015 `, mother defers` FALSE))
#ASSERT REFUSED (`s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` (`fid couple in tax year` 2023 `, one child of both born` 2015 `, mother defers` FALSE))
-- V-5: man, 2023, child born 2015: refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED (`fid the man's points, tax year` 2023 `, child born` 2015 `, mother defers` FALSE)

§ `Independent tests — A1, the claim under (a)(1)`

-- A1-1: salary, non-registered spouse claiming: may claim, and the calculation is made.
#ASSERT `fid may the woman claim, 2024, on 50,000 of` `from employment` `; limb 1` FALSE `; limb 2` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` (`fid 2024, a salaried registered man and, not registered,` (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 100000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE))
-- A1-2: business income from personal exertion.
#ASSERT `fid may the woman claim, 2024, on 50,000 of` `from a business or profession` `; limb 1` FALSE `; limb 2` FALSE
-- A1-3: the REGISTERED spouse claims under (a)(1), the other does not: no (a)(1) calculation.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` (`fid 2024 couple, registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE) `, other` (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 100000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE))
-- A1-4: only income not from personal exertion (rent, dividends): may not claim.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid 2024, a salaried registered man and, not registered,` (`a spouse:` `a woman` `; income from personal exertion` EMPTY `; other income` 50000 `; pre-marriage property income` 0 `; inherited property income` 0 `; claims under (a)` TRUE `; claims under (b)` FALSE `; widowed before this marriage` FALSE `; s 37` FALSE))
-- A1-5: rent within s 1 PE para (7).
#ASSERT `fid may the woman claim, 2024, on 50,000 of` `rent from an asset used for ten years to produce income from personal exertion` `; limb 1` FALSE `; limb 2` FALSE
-- A1-6: retirement grant, s 1 PE para (5): not a pension, no proviso.
#ASSERT `fid may the woman claim, 2024, on 50,000 of` `a grant received on retirement or on death` `; limb 1` FALSE `; limb 2` FALSE
-- A1-7: employer pension, proviso limb 1.
#ASSERT `fid may the woman claim, 2024, on 50,000 of` `a pension paid by a former employer` `; limb 1` TRUE `; limb 2` FALSE
-- A1-8: pension, proviso limb 2 only.
#ASSERT `fid may the woman claim, 2024, on 50,000 of` `a pension from a pension provident fund` `; limb 1` FALSE `; limb 2` TRUE
-- A1-9: pension, neither limb.
#ASSERT NOT `fid may the woman claim, 2024, on 50,000 of` `a pension paid by a former employer` `; limb 1` FALSE `; limb 2` FALSE
-- A1-10, A1-11 (the five-year window at 5 and at 6 years): NOT EXPRESSIBLE.
-- Limb 2 is a BOOLEAN input; the caller decides whether the entitlement fell
-- within "בחמש השנים האחרונות", so the edge is never computed.

§ `Independent tests — D, the common source`

`fid failing (a)` MEANS JUST (`a common source: (a)` FALSE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` FALSE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` FALSE)

-- D-1: all three met, not at home.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` (JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` FALSE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` FALSE)))
-- D-2: (d)(1)(a) fails.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` `fid failing (a)`)
-- D-3: (d)(1)(b) fails, on "התואמת" and then on "ביחס ישיר".
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` (JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` FALSE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` FALSE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` FALSE)))
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` (JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` FALSE `; at home` FALSE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` FALSE)))
-- D-4: at home, permanently, most activity at home.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` (JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` TRUE `; permanent seat` TRUE `; most activity at home` TRUE)))
-- D-5: at home, permanently, most activity elsewhere.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` (JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` TRUE `; permanent seat` TRUE `; most activity at home` FALSE)))
-- D-6: at home, not permanently, most activity at home.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` (JUST (`a common source: (a)` TRUE `; (b) matching` TRUE `; (b) proportional` TRUE `; at home` TRUE `; permanent seat` FALSE `; most activity at home` TRUE)))
-- D-7: no common source.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` NOTHING)
-- D-8: failing common source; the woman's salary is from an unrelated employer.
-- The interface cannot tie an item of income to the common source, so the
-- inputs are those of D-2; the literal (couple) reading answers FALSE.
#ASSERT NOT `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` (`the couple` (`fid 2024, two salaried spouses, the woman claiming, common source` `fid failing (a)`) `, read as` (`this row's readings, but F1 read as` `subsection (a) does not apply to the spouses at all`))
-- D-9: failing common source does not shut (b).
#ASSERT `s 66(b) — the property income is calculated separately:` (`fid spouse` `a woman` `; salary` 120000 `; other income` 0 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 20000 `; claims (a)` TRUE `; claims (b)` TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 66(b) — for` (`spouses in tax year` 2024 `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man` `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE) `; other` (`fid spouse` `a woman` `; salary` 120000 `; other income` 0 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 20000 `; claims (a)` TRUE `; claims (b)` TRUE) `; children` EMPTY `; common source` `fid failing (a)`) `, the property income goes:` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` EQUALS `it is calculated separately on its own`

§ `Independent tests — A2, the income not from personal exertion`

-- A2-1: registered PE higher: the pool goes to the registered spouse.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`fid 2024 couple, registered` (`fid spouse` `a man` `; salary` 300000 `; other income` 30000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` FALSE `; claims (b)` FALSE) `, other` (`fid spouse` `a woman` `; salary` 200000 `; other income` 20000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` TRUE `; claims (b)` FALSE)) EQUALS `registered spouse`
-- A2-2: the non-registered spouse's PE is higher: the pool goes to HER.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`fid 2024 couple, registered` (`fid spouse` `a man` `; salary` 150000 `; other income` 30000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` FALSE `; claims (b)` FALSE) `, other` (`fid spouse` `a woman` `; salary` 250000 `; other income` 20000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` TRUE `; claims (b)` FALSE)) EQUALS `spouse who is not the registered spouse`
-- A2-3: the registered spouse has no PE income.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`fid 2024 couple, registered` (`fid spouse` `a man` `; salary` 0 `; other income` 40000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` FALSE `; claims (b)` FALSE) `, other` (`fid spouse` `a woman` `; salary` 100000 `; other income` 0 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` TRUE `; claims (b)` FALSE)) EQUALS `spouse who is not the registered spouse`
-- A2-4: neither has PE income: the registered spouse.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`fid 2024 couple, registered` (`fid spouse` `a man` `; salary` 0 `; other income` 20000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` FALSE `; claims (b)` FALSE) `, other` (`fid spouse` `a woman` `; salary` 0 `; other income` 20000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 10000 `; claims (a)` FALSE `; claims (b)` TRUE)) EQUALS `registered spouse`
-- A2-5: equal, non-zero PE incomes: refused.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` (`fid 2024 couple, registered` (`fid spouse` `a man` `; salary` 200000 `; other income` 30000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` FALSE `; claims (b)` FALSE) `, other` (`fid spouse` `a woman` `; salary` 200000 `; other income` 20000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` TRUE `; claims (b)` FALSE))
-- A2-6: registered 300,000 + 20,000 + 30,000 = 350,000; separate 200,000.
#ASSERT (`s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` (`fid 2024 couple, registered` (`fid spouse` `a man` `; salary` 300000 `; other income` 20000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` FALSE `; claims (b)` FALSE) `, other` (`fid spouse` `a woman` `; salary` 200000 `; other income` 30000 `; pre-marriage` 0 `; inherited` 0 `; claims (a)` TRUE `; claims (b)` FALSE))) EQUALS (`a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)` 350000 200000 0)

§ `Independent tests — A3, the child's income`

-- A3-1: child turning 17, interest 10,000: the registered spouse's.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(3) — for` (`fid 2024, registered PE` 300000 `, other PE` 200000 `, passive` 0 `, child` (`fid child of both born` 2007 `; transparent company` 0 `; REIT` 0 `; interest` 10000 `; capital gain` 0)) `, the income of this child is the registered spouse's:` (`fid child of both born` 2007 `; transparent company` 0 `; REIT` 0 `; interest` 10000 `; capital gain` 0)
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` (`fid 2024, registered PE` 300000 `, other PE` 200000 `, passive` 0 `, child` (`fid child of both born` 2007 `; transparent company` 0 `; REIT` 0 `; interest` 10000 `; capital gain` 0)) EQUALS 10000
-- A3-2: child turning 18 in 2024: not counted.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` (`fid 2024, registered PE` 300000 `, other PE` 200000 `, passive` 0 `, child` (`fid child of both born` 2006 `; transparent company` 0 `; REIT` 0 `; interest` 10000 `; capital gain` 0)) EQUALS 0
-- A3-3: child turning 19: not counted.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` (`fid 2024, registered PE` 300000 `, other PE` 200000 `, passive` 0 `, child` (`fid child of both born` 2005 `; transparent company` 0 `; REIT` 0 `; interest` 10000 `; capital gain` 0)) EQUALS 0
-- A3-4: capital gains of a child turning 10.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` (`fid 2024, registered PE` 300000 `, other PE` 200000 `, passive` 0 `, child` (`fid child of both born` 2014 `; transparent company` 0 `; REIT` 0 `; interest` 0 `; capital gain` 10000)) EQUALS 10000
-- A3-5: transparent-company income.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` (`fid 2024, registered PE` 300000 `, other PE` 200000 `, passive` 0 `, child` (`fid child of both born` 2014 `; transparent company` 10000 `; REIT` 0 `; interest` 0 `; capital gain` 0)) EQUALS 10000
-- A3-6: REIT income.
#ASSERT `s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` (`fid 2024, registered PE` 300000 `, other PE` 200000 `, passive` 0 `, child` (`fid child of both born` 2014 `; transparent company` 0 `; REIT` 10000 `; interest` 0 `; capital gain` 0)) EQUALS 10000
-- A3-7 (dividends), A3-8 (employment income), A3-9 (linkage differentials as
-- "interest"), A3-11 (interest on inherited assets): NOT EXPRESSIBLE as
-- distinct inputs.  `A child` has no field for dividends or employment income,
-- none distinguishing linkage differentials or discount fees from interest,
-- and none recording that an asset was inherited.  The encoding agrees with
-- A3-7, A3-8 and A3-11 by construction; A3-9 depends on the caller.
-- A3-10: the pool goes to the non-registered spouse (higher PE) and the
-- child's interest to the registered spouse: 150,000 + 10,000 = 160,000;
-- 250,000 + 50,000 = 300,000.
